1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Let's go

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,079
The world glows in color, truth and lies confuse our eyes

5
00:00:30,079 --> 00:00:36,079
Look deep with your heart, the truth's not far apart

6
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:42,079
Hey you could do better, truth and lies can't escape the mind's gray haze

7
00:00:42,079 --> 00:00:48,240
Bring all your courage, and maybe you can save the world

8
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:59,240
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

9
00:01:09,099 --> 00:01:10,200
Love Tycoon

10
00:01:15,099 --> 00:01:17,200
[What is love? A loving heart]

11
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,200
[TV station recruiting temps... Miss MU, the audience's favorite host... interviewing Mr. Meng, Tuna Town's most caring and loving entrepreneur]

12
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:24,200
Tuna Town TV is now recruiting temp field reporters across town

13
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,200
Selected temps will have the chance to work with Miss MU, Tuna Town's most beloved host

14
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:26,200
to interview Mr. Meng, Tuna Town's most big-hearted entrepreneur. Everyone is welcome to sign up!

15
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:52,460
Hey intern, get to work!

16
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:56,020
Now, the live report

17
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:59,240
Charitable entrepreneur Mr. Meng once again spreads the love,

18
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:03,300
inviting every family of three in town to a seaside parent-child summer camp

19
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:07,500
All expenses for this camp are fully sponsored by Mr. Meng

20
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:08,500
Miss MU, film me! We're playing over here!

21
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,960
Mr. Meng believes parents who are always busy working

22
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,400
have no time to play with their kids

23
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,960
and their bond slowly fades away

24
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,939
So he sponsored this camp

25
00:02:22,939 --> 00:02:26,100
to bring kids and parents closer together

26
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:26,900
Hi, kid!

27
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,680
Are you enjoying this summer camp?

28
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,760
I love it!

29
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:31,360
There's tons of yummy food

30
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,700
And lots of games to play

31
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,040
They even gave me this

32
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:35,100
What is it?

33
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:44,760
The fake caterpillar's wriggling frequency

34
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:46,340
is totally different from a real one's

35
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:47,620
Can't you see that?

36
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:54,240
You have no idea how to treat a lady!

37
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,920
That drives me crazy!

38
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,379
Ah, I can't get mad, I can't get mad

39
00:02:57,379 --> 00:02:58,420
Crow's feet, crow's feet!

40
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:00,420
That drives me crazy!

41
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:01,439
That drives me crazy!

42
00:03:01,439 --> 00:03:02,219
I'm leaving now

43
00:03:02,219 --> 00:03:03,280
You keep filming all by yourself

44
00:03:24,599 --> 00:03:25,080
Mrs. Meng

45
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,539
I'm really sorry about this

46
00:03:27,539 --> 00:03:29,360
Sorry for the trouble

47
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:31,680
You're much too polite

48
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:33,460
Mr. Meng still hasn't come back yet

49
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:35,099
Please wait a moment

50
00:03:35,099 --> 00:03:36,020
Okay

51
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:36,759
Madam

52
00:03:36,759 --> 00:03:38,400
We'll just wait a little longer.

53
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:43,599
Please excuse me.

54
00:03:43,599 --> 00:03:44,879
Make yourselves at home.

55
00:03:44,879 --> 00:03:46,360
Mr. Meng will be here shortly.

56
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:48,780
No problem, no problem.

57
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:49,780
Madam, please go ahead.

58
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:54,300
I'm so jealous of Mrs. Meng.

59
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:55,600
Marrying such a wealthy husband,

60
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,380
living in such a beautiful house.

61
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:59,780
She's truly happy.

62
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:04,760
Is this what you think

63
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:06,520
so-called happiness is?

64
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,500
Isn't it?

65
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,500
[After a long time]

66
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:15,900
We've already been waiting here for

67
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:17,980
two hours, forty-nine minutes, and seventeen seconds.

68
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:21,399
Should we keep waiting?

69
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:23,899
He's a big shot, after all.

70
00:04:23,899 --> 00:04:25,079
He must have a lot on his plate.

71
00:04:25,079 --> 00:04:26,939
Let's wait a bit longer.

72
00:04:26,939 --> 00:04:30,819
Mr. Meng

73
00:04:30,819 --> 00:04:32,120
You're back.

74
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:34,420
It's an honor to meet you.

75
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,840
Miss Host.

76
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,620
Sorry to keep you waiting.

77
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:39,840
I'm so happy to see you.

78
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,199
Miss MU.

79
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:43,879
You don't know how much I love watching you.

80
00:04:43,879 --> 00:04:45,519
Watching your show.

81
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:48,919
That's why I specially requested you to interview me.

82
00:04:48,919 --> 00:04:49,759
Really?

83
00:04:49,759 --> 00:04:52,120
You think so highly of me.

84
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,879
Of course.

85
00:04:53,879 --> 00:04:55,000
You're a beauty—hiccup!

86
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:59,219
You seem to have had a lot to drink.

87
00:04:59,219 --> 00:05:00,060
Yeah.

88
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:01,779
Played some cards with a few punks.

89
00:05:01,779 --> 00:05:04,519
Made me lose a fortune.

90
00:05:04,519 --> 00:05:08,839
Shall we start the interview?

91
00:05:08,839 --> 00:05:13,299
Do I look good at this angle?

92
00:05:13,299 --> 00:05:15,359
Will the dim light make my face look gloomy?

93
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,960
Should I touch up my makeup?

94
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:18,920
We can start now.

95
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,520
Mr. Meng.

96
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:22,100
As everyone knows.

97
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:23,420
In Tuna Town.

98
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:27,340
You've planned and sponsored many charity events that benefit society.

99
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:31,660
And you're known as the most loving person in the world.

100
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:35,180
So many people truly, truly admire you.

101
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:37,400
So, if I may ask,

102
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:40,020
what exactly was your reasoning

103
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:43,800
for sponsoring these charity events?

104
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,939
It all goes back to my childhood.

105
00:05:45,939 --> 00:05:47,980
At three, I already knew how to do business.

106
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:48,920
I was very ambitious.

107
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,720
Then I scraped and clawed my way to five.

108
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,079
I even made money off the neighbors.

109
00:05:52,079 --> 00:05:54,819
At six, I taught my teacher to be more caring.

110
00:05:54,819 --> 00:05:57,780
What is he talking about? I'm getting dizzy.

111
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:59,340
He keeps bringing up his childhood.

112
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:00,980
Mr. Meng,

113
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:03,920
could you share something more meaningful from your adult life?

114
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:04,699
Of course.

115
00:06:04,699 --> 00:06:07,060
When I was fifteen,

116
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:10,199
all the girls around me were smitten.

117
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:15,000
Is this guy out of his mind?

118
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,719
Mr. Meng, this is bad!

119
00:06:16,719 --> 00:06:19,740
Your son was kidnapped on his way home from school.

120
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:23,199
By sixteen, I was already making big money.

121
00:06:23,199 --> 00:06:24,139
Huh? What?

122
00:06:24,139 --> 00:06:33,379
I never thought even Officer Han would be helpless.

123
00:06:36,099 --> 00:06:37,659
There are still no leads on the kidnappers.

124
00:06:37,659 --> 00:06:39,560
The police can only keep close watch,

125
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:41,879
waiting for the kidnappers' next ransom demand.

126
00:06:41,879 --> 00:06:43,060
They've made their move again.

127
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:46,360
The criminals managed to evade the many bodyguards around Mr. Meng's son

128
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:47,360
and complete the kidnapping.

129
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:49,620
They must know him quite well.

130
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:55,199
Mr. Meng, please don't be upset.

131
00:06:55,199 --> 00:06:57,560
The police will definitely rescue your son.

132
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,740
Yes, yes.

133
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:04,060
Didn't you want to interview me?

134
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:06,939
Why not come to my disco dance hall?

135
00:07:06,939 --> 00:07:08,620
We can dance happily

136
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:10,300
while you interview me.

137
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:19,120
Huh? Did he forget his son was just kidnapped?

138
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,439
This guy is really...

139
00:07:21,439 --> 00:07:24,420
Is this what he calls love?

140
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:27,060
What love?

141
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:28,959
I think he's heartless.

142
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Ugh, so classless.

143
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,079
Thank you for bringing him back.

144
00:07:40,079 --> 00:07:44,819
Hello, Mrs. Meng.

145
00:07:44,819 --> 00:07:47,300
Mr. Meng is drunk.

146
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,759
You've really gone through trouble.

147
00:07:49,759 --> 00:07:51,959
He's always like this.

148
00:07:51,959 --> 00:07:53,420
He often gets dead drunk.

149
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:56,019
Mrs. Meng?

150
00:07:56,019 --> 00:07:58,379
It seems neither you nor Mr. Meng are very worried.

151
00:07:58,379 --> 00:07:59,740
Your own son's been kidnapped.

152
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:04,819
Going by the usual crime pattern,

153
00:08:04,819 --> 00:08:06,160
once the kidnappers take the target,

154
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,100
they're bound to demand a ransom.

155
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:08,780
But there's been no word at all.

156
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:09,860
That's highly unusual.

157
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:12,720
I don't know anything about that,

158
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,960
but I'm very worried about the child's safety.

159
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:17,520
Don't worry, Mrs. Meng.

160
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:19,340
We assure you your child

161
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:21,900
will come back to you safe and sound.

162
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:25,180
Well, it's getting late.

163
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:27,800
We'll head back and prepare to continue interviewing Mr. Meng tomorrow.

164
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:40,100
Sir? Sir!

165
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:43,100
What is it?

166
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:44,100
Waking me up this early.

167
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,100
Your call.

168
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:48,100
Hello?

169
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:49,100
Mr. Meng.

170
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:50,100
Your son is in our hands.

171
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:52,100
If you want him to get back alive, do what we say.

172
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:54,100
You just want money, right?

173
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:56,100
I've got plenty!

174
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:14,300
Temp.

175
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,180
What's your problem now?

176
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:19,019
Someone's starting to make ransom calls

177
00:09:19,019 --> 00:09:22,259
Wait!

178
00:09:22,259 --> 00:09:23,259
[Ending Theme]

179
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:43,980
Life's bound to have its unhappy moments

180
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:51,540
Saying goodbye to today always stings a little

181
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:59,279
Look at tomorrow waving to me from your horizon

182
00:09:59,279 --> 00:10:03,000
Every day is just sunrise and sunset

183
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,940
Drifting into time, dreaming of more

184
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:12,040
Longing for every second, every moment of life

185
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:18,760
Bright eyes are sparkling

186
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:22,140
A smile that faces the sun

187
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:29,740
Brave enough to speak the little feelings hidden in your heart

188
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:34,180
Music blows in the morning breeze

189
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:37,500
Carrying away years of wishes

190
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:42,720
It will quietly wait at every crossroads

191
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:50,440
It will quietly wait at every crossroads